      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e7f5bed6",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: hi_hacker_bro_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a crowd of men, many wearing traditional Middle Eastern head coverings, with the text 'hi hacker bro' and 'we are muslim brotherhood'. The intent is to associate the Muslim Brotherhood with hackers, implying a negative or threatening connotation. This is a hateful meme because it uses the image of a real political and religious organization to stereotype and vilify a group of people based on their identity, potentially inciting fear or hostility toward Muslims or the Muslim Brotherhood. The juxtaposition of the image of a peaceful or solemn gathering with the mocking 'hacker bro' label is designed to dehumanize and demonize the group, fitting within the category of Islamophobia as it links the group with negative stereotypes (e.g., terrorism, criminality, or being a threat to digital security).",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_05a9578f"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
